.TH CVECTOR_CREATE_FULL 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cvector_create_full \- create a vector with custom memory management
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

cvec cvector_create_full(size_t elem_size,
                         ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *mmgmt_procs,
                         char **err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Creates a new vector container. The caller sets every memory management
option. The vector stores elements of the given size. It controls its
capacity by itself.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
elem_size     Size of each element in bytes (must be > 0, and must not
              exceed SIZE_MAX / 4)
mmgmt_procs   Custom memory management procedures, or NULL for
              default malloc/free
err           Optional pointer to receive error string on failure
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns a pointer to the new vector on success
Returns NULL on failure. An elem_size of 0 is a failure. An elem_size
that makes the allocation of the first 4-element backing buffer
overflow is also a failure
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The first capacity is 4 elements
Capacity scaling: 2x when full, 0.5x when less than 1/4 full
Minimum capacity: 4 elements
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvector_create (3),
.BR cvector_destroy (3)
